WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.939
ProofKey is a work-treasury prototype for contractor teams.

00:00:02.939 --> 00:00:05.878
It follows agreed outcomes from approval to payment.

00:00:05.878 --> 00:00:10.287
This Guided Demo uses test CTC, practice tokens on a test network.

00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:13.593
It is not a bank payout or real earnings.

00:00:14.343 --> 00:00:18.206
The recorded program starts with one hundred twenty test CTC.

00:00:18.206 --> 00:00:23.615
Thirty test CTC is reserved for the first job, and forty for the second.

00:00:23.615 --> 00:00:24.774
Fifty stays unassigned.

00:00:24.774 --> 00:00:27.092
Reserved means set aside, not paid.

00:00:27.842 --> 00:00:33.971
When the first outcome is approved, thirty becomes owed, but it is not paid yet.

00:00:33.971 --> 00:00:35.606
Ethereum records the outcome.

00:00:35.606 --> 00:00:37.649
Attestcoin authenticates that source record.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:40.101
Creditcoin then recognizes the payment right.

00:00:40.101 --> 00:00:43.371
Withdrawal sends test tokens to the agreed wallet.

00:00:43.371 --> 00:00:46.640
Evidence crosses chains; the budget stays on Creditcoin.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:51.253
The program’s authenticateBatch transaction succeeded on Creditcoin’s test network.

00:00:51.253 --> 00:00:55.116
The captured receipt identifies the transaction and its block.

00:00:55.116 --> 00:00:56.833
This success authenticates records.

00:00:56.833 --> 00:01:01.555
It does not judge work quality and does not withdraw funds.

00:01:02.305 --> 00:01:07.471
The native BlockProver emitted TransactionVerified for the recorded Ethereum position and a second record.

00:01:07.471 --> 00:01:10.423
The screen shows the source height and index.

00:01:10.423 --> 00:01:12.637
Authentication proves the records were checked.

00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:15.958
It does not judge work quality or withdraw funds.

00:01:16.708 --> 00:01:19.694
Both sides settle the second job at twenty-five.

00:01:19.694 --> 00:01:22.307
The released fifteen supports a follow-up job.

00:01:22.307 --> 00:01:25.292
Its recorded no-delivery result frees that fifteen again.

00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:27.905
This is not a unilateral buyer reduction.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:33.932
The completed records show thirty plus twenty-five, or fifty-five, sent to work.

00:01:33.932 --> 00:01:38.330
Fifty plus fifteen, or sixty-five, returns to the funding account.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:41.408
One hundred twenty equals fifty-five plus sixty-five.

00:01:41.408 --> 00:01:43.168
Network gas is separate.

00:01:43.918 --> 00:01:47.261
This captured withdrawFor receipt is one recorded work-payment transfer.

00:01:47.261 --> 00:01:52.833
A team member, the worker, or another submitter can send the evidence and pay gas.

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:55.805
The public withdrawal cannot redirect the agreed destination.

00:01:56.555 --> 00:02:00.048
Disputes use illustrated rules, separate from the recorded budget.

00:02:00.048 --> 00:02:04.318
Three reviewers are named, and two matching votes settle a challenge.

00:02:04.318 --> 00:02:08.976
If no ruling arrives by the source-block cutoff, someone must submit timeout.

00:02:08.976 --> 00:02:13.246
The example restores capacity; it does not automatically pay or refund.

00:02:13.996 --> 00:02:17.572
Inspect the no-wallet demo, repository, and recorded receipts.

00:02:17.572 --> 00:02:21.595
Next come independent repeat use and external security review.

00:02:21.595 --> 00:02:25.172
This is not a production or adoption claim.

00:02:25.172 --> 00:02:31.431
